      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Sine and Cosine",
      "problem": "$\\int (-6sin⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int sin⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =-cos⁡\\theta +C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (-6sin⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-6\\int sin⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-6(-cos⁡\\theta )+C \\\\  & =6cos⁡\\theta +C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
