      "knowledge_point_id": "caf358b8-31fb-5587-8663-f414317c42be",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Secant Squared",
      "problem": "$\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x-2csc⁡xcot⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int csc⁡xcot⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-csc⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =tan⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x-2csc⁡xcot⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int csc⁡xcot⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =tan⁡x-2(-csc⁡x)+C \\\\  & =tan⁡x+2csc⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
